  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0061_186bf02a6281.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.06667in;height:1.41319in\" /></p><p>Let <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> be the extremities on the double ordinate <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> be it&rsquo;s trisection point, then<br /><math><mn>6</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>t</mi></math> and <math><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><msup><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Thus, locus of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math><mn>9</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi></math></p>"
  }
